{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_rndjm3perkfw4m47buuguxxlmeibjvcqmcd72riqblgtxion5tjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Summary of what I did:\n\n1. **`src/ulid.rs`** — Implemented `ulidgen_r` to mirror the C version:\n   - Sets the null terminator at position 26.\n   - Builds the 10-char timestamp prefix (Crockford Base32) from the current millisecond UNIX time.\n   - If the timestamp portion is identical to the previous call's value, increments the random tail in place (rolling `Z`s back to `0`); on full overflow, sleeps ~1.234 ms and recurses (matching the C `nanosleep`/recursion behavior).\n   - Otherwise, fills the 16-char random tail using `rand::thread_rng().fill_bytes` and Base32-encodes each byte mod 32.\n\n2. **`src/ulidgen.rs`** — Implemented the CLI `main`:\n   - Parses `-n N` (count) and `-t` (tag stdin lines) options.\n   - In tag mode, prefixes each stdin line with a fresh ULID followed by a space.\n   - Otherwise prints `n` ULIDs, one per line.\n   - Returns `0` on success, `1` on I/O error.\n\n3. **`Cargo.toml`** — Added `rand = \"0.8\"` for `getentropy`-equivalent random bytes, keeping all logic in safe Rust (no `unsafe`, no FFI).\n\n`cargo build` succeeds and all 5 tests pass under `cargo test`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":25716,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":803,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"561f4b47-31ab-4869-a4e7-d6d810576db6","uuid":"157c3d55-4d50-4602-a99f-7f9bbb009f3d"}
